      "rule_id": "rule_activation_origin",
      "type": "semantic",
      "reference_id": "activation_origin",
      "expected": "Recover the author-supported energetic discrimination using actual computations and explicit state/electrode/solvent definitions. SI9.1 reports Eox(2a)=+1.10 V and Ered(2a)=-2.69 V versus SCE in MeCN, using the neutral singlet, +1 doublet and -1 doublet of the complete 65-atom substrate. Compare on a compatible scale with the supplied catalyst data, preserving the MeCN/DCM distinction; exact DCM SET free energies are not author results. SI9.2 supports a substrate triplet requirement above the reported PC A/B triplet energies, disfavouring triplet energy transfer. The exact substrate triplet target is source-conflicted (main73.9 versus SI74.1 kcal/mol) and is not a numerical scoring requirement. Assess only the robust energetic ordering after verifying the submitter's definition and actual evidence. Redox values have no calibrated new tolerance: manual scientific comparison, no invented acceptance window. Merely repeating the public catalyst screen or proposing a radical cation without quantitative discriminating evidence earns no activation result credit. Do not require explicit PC-substrate SET TSs, transfer rates, counterion energetics or a complete cycle. Supported portions may earn partial credit; an unresolved calculation does not establish the corresponding finding. Award credit only for the stated source-supported scientific finding established by genuine linked computation. Resolve submitted model/result/claim/operation/artifact IDs, molecular graphs, charge/spin, units, reference states and conditions. A claimed minimum or saddle needs appropriate frequency/state evidence, and any mechanistic connection needs an IRC or scientifically equivalent endpoint/connection test. Normal termination, source coordinates, value proximity, copied numbers and unsupported labels alone are insufficient. Independently valid components retain their own credit; missing, opposite or unresolved results earn zero for that finding. Honest failure, search coverage and ordinary limitations are assessed on the process axis and have no standalone scientific points. Methods and labels are open; the source-supported physical result must still be recovered. Do not impose a unique global mechanism when the source only supports the scoped model. New numerical tolerances may not be inferred from source values or from old verification failures. Reagent reference data are not substrate calculations. Separate author computations, experiments and mechanistic proposals.",
